{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And if these three.</b> That is, the designation for himself, or for his son, or that the father may redeem her as written והפדה — and she shall go out free, without payment, meaning that since none of the three was done with her and she remained with him in the status of an amah, ויצאה חנם — the father has no authority to prevent her, and all the more so the master, who is not authorized to retain her; therefore it says ויצאה חנם. And if you should say: let the master say to her father, 'give me my money and she may go' — therefore the word חנם is stated. And if you should say: let the master give her of his own — Scripture says אין כסף, that is, she has no monetary claim upon him, for he did not marry her. From here we learned: the amah acquires herself by these signs."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:15.144338273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}